WEBVTT

NOTE Captions are also burned into the supplied MP4.

00:00:02.556 --> 00:00:05.892
NARRATOR: Every systematic review begins with a perfectly reasonable
request.

00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:11.200
PI: Just a quick review.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.390
PI: Shouldn't take long.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.388
NARRATOR: Then the abstracts arrive.

00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:18.432
NARRATOR: The search was comprehensive.

00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:21.145
NARRATOR: Unfortunately, so were the consequences.

00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:23.216
NARRATOR: Welcome to Club Eligibility.

00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:24.320
NARRATOR: Full text upstairs.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.998
NARRATOR: The generative model arrives with an entourage, a limousine, and
the ability to turn

00:00:29.998 --> 00:00:31.941
NARRATOR: one screening decision into a TED Talk.

00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:40.172
LLM: Before deciding whether to retain this abstract, we must
consider the epistemological

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:41.524
LLM: status of relevance.

00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:46.456
LIBRARIAN: You've written more about whether to read the abstract than the
authors wrote in the

00:00:46.456 --> 00:00:47.516
LIBRARIAN: abstract.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.705
NARRATOR: Jev arrives with a folding stool.

00:00:52.705 --> 00:00:54.059
NARRATOR: Jev does decisions.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.043
NARRATOR: Give this zero-shot classifier the title, abstract, and
eligibility criteria.

00:01:00.043 --> 00:01:02.550
NARRATOR: It returns a structured decision with probabilities.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.964
NARRATOR: No bespoke training.

00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:05.519
NARRATOR: No free-text monologue.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.720
NARRATOR: Here, one question orders the queue for human screening.

00:01:08.446 --> 00:01:10.739
NARRATOR: Eight diagnostic test accuracy reviews.

00:01:10.739 --> 00:01:14.311
NARRATOR: Twenty-six thousand, eight hundred and thirty-two records with
abstracts.

00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:17.120
NARRATOR: Mean WSS at ninety-five: zero point six six one.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.959
NARRATOR: That's work saved over sampling at ninety-five percent recall,
measured

00:01:20.959 --> 00:01:22.463
NARRATOR: retrospectively.

00:01:22.463 --> 00:01:24.016
NARRATOR: It isn't accuracy.

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.054
NARRATOR: Performance varies by review.

00:01:26.054 --> 00:01:28.620
NARRATOR: The article reports a bill of about one dollar forty-six.

00:01:29.153 --> 00:01:34.477
LIBRARIAN: Finally, research infrastructure we can expense without forming
a steering committee.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.388
NARRATOR: The published three-model ensemble does better: zero point six
eight zero.

00:01:40.388 --> 00:01:43.953
NARRATOR: Add embedding reranking: zero point seven zero eight.

00:01:43.953 --> 00:01:47.422
NARRATOR: Jev remains impressively competitive for something with less
furniture.

00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:51.145
LIBRARIAN: Three models, one decision.

00:01:51.145 --> 00:01:53.683
LIBRARIAN: A committee meeting with measurable output.

00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:54.988
LIBRARIAN: Unsettling.

00:01:54.988 --> 00:01:57.620
LIBRARIAN: Please record this unprecedented event in the minutes.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.112
NARRATOR: These are published benchmark comparisons, using older models.

00:02:02.112 --> 00:02:04.173
NARRATOR: Today's competitors may change the picture.

00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:09.069
NARRATOR: Management spots an opportunity for improvement.

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:13.198
NARRATOR: Replace the single overall question with five criterion
questionnaires.

00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:15.173
NARRATOR: Five times the judgements.

00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:16.720
NARRATOR: Surely that means better screening?

00:02:17.351 --> 00:02:21.397
NARRATOR: In this tested setup, the probability-based expected-score
variant reaches only zero

00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:23.163
NARRATOR: point five three six.

00:02:23.163 --> 00:02:24.534
NARRATOR: More machinery.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.320
NARRATOR: Worse ranking.

00:02:25.941 --> 00:02:29.605
LIBRARIAN: We added bureaucracy and performance got worse.

00:02:29.605 --> 00:02:32.400
LIBRARIAN: Finally, AI understands academia.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.597
NARRATOR: The questions or scoring might be the problem.

00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:37.421
NARRATOR: That's a hypothesis.

00:02:37.421 --> 00:02:39.320
NARRATOR: Decomposition hasn't been convicted.

00:02:41.343 --> 00:02:43.338
LIBRARIAN: One question.

00:02:43.338 --> 00:02:45.917
LIBRARIAN: How do you know when to stop screening?

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.619
NARRATOR: The evaluator consults the known benchmark labels.

00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:55.655
NARRATOR: Those labels locate the ninety-five percent recall point after
scoring.

00:02:55.655 --> 00:02:57.519
NARRATOR: Jev never sees them.

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:01.020
NARRATOR: A retrospective result doesn't give a new review a validated
stopping rule.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.851
LIBRARIAN: Excellent crystal ball.

00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:07.259
LIBRARIAN: Does it work before we know which studies are relevant?

00:03:07.259 --> 00:03:10.908
LIBRARIAN: My protocol has a surprisingly strict policy on clairvoyance.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.987
NARRATOR: Before trusting automated exclusions, prospectively validate
thresholds, calibration,

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:17.452
NARRATOR: and stopping rules.

00:03:17.452 --> 00:03:19.349
NARRATOR: Test other review types too.

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:22.072
NARRATOR: A probability needs checking, and eight DTA reviews aren't the
whole

00:03:22.072 --> 00:03:23.420
NARRATOR: evidence-synthesis universe.

00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:25.832
PAPER: The methods are in the full text.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.955
LIBRARIAN: Of course they are.

00:03:30.955 --> 00:03:33.781
LIBRARIAN: Heaven forbid the abstract become useful.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.668
NARRATOR: Jev works the queue.

00:03:39.668 --> 00:03:41.693
NARRATOR: The librarian keeps the keys.

00:03:41.693 --> 00:03:43.112
NARRATOR: Cheap decisions.

00:03:43.112 --> 00:03:44.220
NARRATOR: Expensive questions.
